      "title": "Maine Maritime Academy",
      "description": "Academic Leadership and Faculty - Academics - Academics - Maine Maritime Academy Maine Maritime Academy A COLLEGE OF ENGINEERING, BUSINESS, SCIENCE, AND TRANSPORTATION Buttons skip to main content Main Menu Admissions & Aid General Information Undergraduate Admissions Meet the Staff Graduate Admissions Center for Professional Mariner Development Visit Financial Aid Academics Academics Departments Academic Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Hands-On Education Waterfront Research Navy ROTC Academic Services Library Undergraduate Catalog Academic Calendar Commencement Academic Leadership & Faculty Ethics Across the Curriculum Accreditation Center for Professional Mariner Development Student Life Student Life Residential Life Sponsor Family Program Student Activities You Belong Here Student Government Association Athletics & Recreation Regimental Program Health & Counseling Services Dining Services Campus Safety Campus Bookstore Community Standards Campus Resources New Student Information Title IX Alumni Alumni Alumni Association Stay Connected Get Involved Events Benefits and Services Awards and Recognition Eight Bells Alumni Business Directory Legacy Paver Project Yearbooks Giving Give Online Events Planned Giving Yacht Donation Program Annual Fund Ways to Give Annual Giving Report The Maine Maritime Academy Foundation Scholarships Parents Association Completed Campaigns Alumni Association Contact Us About About MMA Office of the President Communications Conference Services Employment at MMA Visit MMA Calendar Campus Directory NSMV Updates Strategic Plan Contact Us Section Menu Academics Departments Academic Programs Graduate Programs Online Hands-On Education TSSOM Training Cruise Bowdoin Training Cruise Field Experience Waterfront Training Ship State of Maine Tug Pentagoet Schooner Bowdoin Research IRB for Research involving Human Subjects Navy ROTC Academic Services Support Services Registrar’s Office Career Services Library Undergraduate Catalog Academic Calendar Commencement Academic Leadership and Faculty Office of the Provost Excellence in Teaching Award Ethics Across the Curriculum Accreditation Center for Professional Mariner Development Home > Academics > Academic Leadership and Faculty Academic Leadership & Faculty Jennifer K. Waters, Ph.D. is Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost. Laurie Flood is Professor of Engineering and Dean of Faculty. Professors at Maine Maritime Academy work with students in classrooms, laboratories, and aboard ships. Our full-time faculty of more than 60 men and women stress the connections between theory and real-world applications. Faculty come from diverse academic backgrounds, and from industrial positions in engineering, ship operations, marine science, maritime management, and small vessel design and operation. Faculty members serve as academic advisors and also participate in research, consulting, and other academic pursuits. Part-time faculty include visiting professors from industry and from domestic and foreign universities. Faculty by Academic Departments – Fall 2026 * – Denotes Department Chair (s) –  Denotes Sabbatical Italic – Denotes faculty not teaching Arts & Sciences Audette, Priscilla Avery, David * Baker, Cirila Batt, Thomas Boal, Jeffrey Boman, Misty Bonaminio, Deb Boucher, Joceline Burkholder, Brandon Ciampa, David Coe, Carolyn Delicata, Janelle Feeley, Roger Jensen, Michael Kingsbury, Aaron Kingston, Andrew Kremelberg, David Lapham, Gary Merritt, Karen Moser, Joseph (Jody) Nyberg, Amy Omlor, Heidi Pease, Jeremiah Polojärvi, Dana Quinby, Emma Ravan, Vernon (Fred) Rice, Rachel Simmons, Jacob (s) Skwiot, Christine Stwertka, Alexander (Zanny) Taub, Jeffrey Torre, Jaime Turok, Katharine VanSpronsen, Hillary Zmek, Nathaniel Harold Alfond School of Engineering Anderson, Amanda Boidi, Ronald Bradshaw, Nathaniel Christian, Laurel Ciampa, Joe Davis, Marsden Ferden, Scott Flood, Laurie , Dean of Faculty Hersom, Rory Hubbard, Leon Kokkulunk,