      "title": "Maine Maritime Academy",
      "description": "Staff Positions - Employment at MMA - Employment at MMA - Maine Maritime Academy Maine Maritime Academy A COLLEGE OF ENGINEERING, BUSINESS, SCIENCE, AND TRANSPORTATION Buttons skip to main content Main Menu Admissions & Aid General Information Undergraduate Admissions Meet the Staff Graduate Admissions Center for Professional Mariner Development Visit Financial Aid Academics Academics Departments Academic Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Hands-On Education Waterfront Research Navy ROTC Academic Services Library Undergraduate Catalog Academic Calendar Commencement Academic Leadership & Faculty Ethics Across the Curriculum Accreditation Center for Professional Mariner Development Student Life Student Life Residential Life Sponsor Family Program Student Activities You Belong Here Student Government Association Athletics & Recreation Regimental Program Health & Counseling Services Dining Services Campus Safety Campus Bookstore Community Standards Campus Resources New Student Information Title IX Alumni Alumni Alumni Association Stay Connected Get Involved Events Benefits and Services Awards and Recognition Eight Bells Alumni Business Directory Legacy Paver Project Yearbooks Giving Give Online Events Planned Giving Yacht Donation Program Annual Fund Ways to Give Annual Giving Report The Maine Maritime Academy Foundation Scholarships Parents Association Completed Campaigns Alumni Association Contact Us About About MMA Office of the President Communications Conference Services Employment at MMA Visit MMA Calendar Campus Directory NSMV Updates Strategic Plan Contact Us Section Menu Employment at MMA Staff Positions Faculty Positions Cruise Positions Human Resources Benefits Information HR Policies HR Forms Wellness Program Maine Maritime Academy > Employment at MMA > Staff Positions Staff Positions The salary range listed reflects the full range established for the positions. At Maine Maritime Academy (MMA) base pay depends on a variety of factors, including the responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s education, relevant experience, knowledge, skills, internal equity, and available funding, where applicable. Compensation is only one part of MMA’s total rewards package. Eligible employees may enjoy a comprehensive benefits program that includes health, dental, and vision insurance; retirement plan contributions; paid time off; professional development opportunities; tuition benefits where applicable; and access to a variety of wellness and employee support programs. FULL-TIME Title Status Starting Salary Building and Grounds Maintenance Worker (Custodian) Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $19.60 - $21.56/hour Building & Grounds Maintenance Mechanic & Trades Worker I Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $22.78 - $25.15/hour Building & Grounds Maintenance Mechanic & Trades Worker II Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $26.36 - $29.19/hour Building & Grounds Maintenance Mechanic & Trades Worker III Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $28.66 - $31.79/hour Campus Safety Officer I Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $22.85 - $24.43/hour Counselor Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $65,119.80 $72,406.02/year Director of Alumni Relations Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $80,000.00 - $100,000.00/year Education and Engagement Librarian Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $62,254.40 - $69,035.20/year Electrician - TSSOM Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $72,134.40 - $80,225.60/year Lead Instructor & Course Developer- Fire Training & Vessel Navigation Operations Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $91,395.20 - $101,836.80/year Master, Small Craft - Waterfront Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $61,214.40 - $67,932.80/year Master, Tug Pentagoet Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $71,059.20 – $76,625.89/year Network Service Manager Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $83,595.20 - $93,080.00/year Plumber - TSSOM Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $76,523.20 - $85,113.60/year Purchasing Operation Technician Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $25.28 - $27.99/hour Second Assistant Engineer - TSSOM Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $92,788.80 - $103,459.20/year Sailing Technician - Assistant Sailing Coach Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $57,886.40 - $61,963.20/year User Support Technician - Brunswick Campus Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $25.59 - $27.37/hour Soft-money temporary appointment through 8/31/2027 PART-TIME Title Status Starting Salary Campus Safety Officer Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $18.00/hour Deck Maintenance Assistant Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $25.00/hour Engine Maintenance Assistant Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $25.00/hour TEMPORARY Title Status Starting Salary Watch Officer - Engineer (in-port) Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $450 - $500/day depending on license Head Men's Golf Coach Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $8,000.00/year Assistant Swimming & Diving Coach for 2026-2027 season Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Assistant Football Coach for 2026-2027 season Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Assistant Golf Coach for 2026-2027 season Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Assistant Women's Lacrosse Coach for 2026-2027 season Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Assistant Women's Soccer Coach for 2026-2027 season Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Assistant Men's Wrestling Coach for 2026-2027 season Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach for 2026-2027 season Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Fire Training Assistant Lab Instructor – Fall 2026 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $7,000.00/semester Fire Fighting Assistant - On-Call 2026-2027 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $25.00/hour EMS Rehab Officer 2026-2027 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $35.00/hour Fire Fighting Instructor 2026-2027 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $35.00/hour Fire Fighting Safety Officer 2026-2027 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $35.00/hour Fire Fighting Lecturer Instructor 2026-2027 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $50.00/hour Center for Professional Mariner Development (CPMD) Instructor 2026-2027 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $50.00/hour Center for Professional Mariner Development Lead Instructor / Course Developer 2026-2027 Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $50.00/hour Life Guard Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $15.10/hour Testing and Tutoring Assistant Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $18.00 - $21.00/hour Second Mate - Schooner Bowdoin Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $174.24/day Third Mate - Schooner Bowdoin Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $174.24/day Steward - Schooner Bowdoin Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $174.24/day INTERNAL Title Status Starting Salary Network Service Manager Now Hiring, Accepting Applications $83,595.20 - $93,080.00/year ONGOING Hiring for these positions is postponed until further notice. Clerical Pool Temporary Utility Worker Pool (various departments) On-Call Nurse How to Apply Interested individuals should submit a cover letter and resume including contact information for at least three professional references using the online Employment Application . PLEASE NOTE THAT INCOMPLETE SUBMISSIONS WILL NOT BE CONSIDERED. All offers are made contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background investigation. Individuals cruising onboard our ships are also required to undergo a pre-employment drug-screening. To submit additional employment forms, please use our Employee Document Upload Form . Tobacco-Free Notice For the health and wellbeing of our community, the Maine Maritime Academy campus and vessels (ashore and afloat) are smoke- and tobacco-free as of August 1, 2016. Smoke and Tobacco Free Campus Policy (effective 8/1/16) Equal Employment Opportunities Maine Maritime Academy is an equal opportunity employer.  The Academy complies with federal and/or state law that prohibit unlawful discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ethnicity, ancestry, marital status, disability, age, genetic information or veteran status.  The Academy provides reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals upon request. Women, minorities, and veterans are strongly encouraged to apply. MMA is unable at this time to sponsor visas. We welcome foreign nationals with valid U.S. work authorization to apply. Contact Us Human Resources Nicole Dyer Human Resources Generalist 207-326-2665 nicole.dyer@mma.edu Apply for Employment MAINE MARITIME ACADEMY | 1 PLEASANT STREET, CASTINE, ME 04420 | 207-326-4311 | EMAIL: ADMISSIONS@MMA.EDU Campus Safety Mariners Athletics Map & Directions Mobile App News Webcam MyMMA NSMV Updates Social Media at MMA All Rights Reserved © 2026 • Web issue? Non-Discrimination Notice • Privacy Policy & GDPR"
